## Worksheet

**F1 — Core loop**: `G` object; `makeRng()` seeded PRNG used everywhere (no Math.random found); `resolveTurnCore`→hazard→production→needs→fatigue→morale, then `triggerEvent`→`finishTurn` in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 — Map**: `genMap()` builds 8x8 via `pickWeighted(G.rng,...)`; `canBuildAt` checks `def.terrain.includes(tile.terrain)`; `neighborTerrainMatch` adjacency adds to `base` in `resolveProduction`. Score 2.

**F3 — Economy**: mine→forge (ore→metal), composter→greenhouse (ash(ambient)→soil→food); `storageCap`/`addRes` enforce caps and log overflow. Score 2.

**F4 — Population**: colonist records with skill/fatigue/morale/job/assigned; `skillFactor(worker.skill)`, `fatigueFactor(worker.fatigue)` read in `resolveProduction`. Score 2.

**F5 — Needs**: `resolveNeeds` consumes food/water, shortage lowers morale via `delta`; `moraleFactor(worker.morale)` used in production ratio; +2 morale/turn recovery when met. Score 2.

**F6 — Research**: 9 nodes in `RESEARCH`; `canResearch` enforces `prereq.every`; `purchaseResearch` deducts cost; `condenserMult`/`generatorMult`/`stormMitigation`/`repairDiscount` all read elsewhere. Score 2.

**F7 — Events**: 12 events in `EVENTS`; `pickWeighted` selection; 5 choice events (wandererArrives, contaminatedWater, colonistDispute, ashLungSickness, raiderSkirmish); `eventState[id]` cooldown tracked/reset. Score 2.

**F8 — Trade**: `buyPrice` uses stock ratio + `market.drift`; `inventory` qty decremented in `tradeBuy`; `tradeSell` implemented and both wired to buttons. Score 2.

**F9 — Hazard**: `resolveHazard` fires on `turn%8===0`, severity grows with turn; `damageFactor(b.damage)` reduces production; windbreak/`stormShelters`/`reinforced` reduce mitigation; `repairBuilding` spends parts. Score 2.

**F10 — Save/load**: `serializeState`→JSON to textarea; `loadBtn` parses via `JSON.parse`, `validateSaveObj` checks fields, error shown in `loadMsg`. Score 2.

**F11 — End conditions**: `checkEndConditions` has both win (turn≥60, pop≥12, no shortage) and lose (pop=0) branches, called every `finishTurn`; `computeScore` combines pop/research/stock/turns; `showEndScreen` renders summary. Score 2.

**F12 — UI**: `switchTab` wired to nav buttons; `pushLog` stores `turn`, shown as `T${e.turn}`; `attachTooltip`/`resTooltipHtml`/`tileTooltipHtml` explain numbers; Space/1-5 keydown handlers; `@media(max-width:480px)` layout. Score 2.

**F13 — Dev panel**: `runTests` asserts cap enforcement, PRNG determinism, save/load hash equality, invariant bounds (not trivial); `runBenchmark` runs 200 headless turns via `endTurnAuto`, prints `stateHash`. Score 2.

**G1**: `RESEARCH.efficientCondensers.condenserMult`/`geothermal.generatorMult` read via `G.research.done` in `resolveProduction`, multiply `yieldMult` into `addRes` amount every turn. Score 4.

**G2**: `resolveNeeds` shortage writes `c.morale` delta; `moraleFactor(worker.morale)` factors into `ratio` in `resolveProduction`, applied every turn. Score 4.

**G3**: `resolveHazard` sets `b.damage`; `damageFactor(b.damage)` cuts `ratio`; `repairBuilding` spends parts, resets `damage=0` restoring output. Score 4.

**G4**: `buyPrice` reads `G.res[res]/cap` (stockpile) and `G.market.drift[res]` (random-walked each turn in `updateMarketForNewTurn`). Score 4.

**G5**: `wandererArrives`, `contaminatedWater`, `colonistDispute`, `ashLungSickness`, `raiderSkirmish` choice branches each mutate `res`/`colonists`/`morale` differently, not just log text. Score 4.

